A) Rule can have statuses
active/expired/cancelled/deprecated
active - is created and can be considered for all future month projections.
expired - end date over and hence not to be included for projections
cancelled - user cancelled the rule
deprectaed - new version is available and projections possible only if the occurence does not overlap into newer versions projection.
[when a newer version is created a user may say that the newer version start date after 4 months and if the original rule repeat = Monthly then 
it should be projected for those gap period until the start date for new version. so effectively when a new version is created and a start date is mentioned 
for it then the end date for the old version falls just before it.]
B) rule should have configuratgion to mark whether it is never ending or if here is an end date.
C) Repeat to have enumeration = {monthly, quarterly, yearly} 
1)Action: configure a new rule
name=netflix
amount=1000
category=Lifestyle
Type=Expense
Repeats=Monthly
Day of Month = 1
Effective From=26-09-2026

This create s rule with version = v1.
result: planned entry for 1-Oct and onwards every Month

2) Action - Editing rule name = netflix
change the amount = 1100
or Repeats = Yearly
or Day of Month = 5 (for instance)

result:
new rule version is created as V2 with status = active
rule version v1 status=deprecated
every month will start using these rule for projections.

3) Action: Edit Rule 
name=netflix-new
or Category = Housing
or type = income


Result:
creates another rule and not a version.
the parent rule version remains as cancelled.
all unplanned items for each month will be driven from updated active rules again.
in this case the parent rule instances will be removed and new rule with active status is kept.


Note: an end date for rule will normally be marked only if a new version created or the rule
 status changed to cancelled